<Step ID="2" Task="What does condition (ii) of a saddle pair (R,C) mean in terms of column dominance?" Difficulty="4" Token="50" Rely=""/>
<Step ID="3" Task="If (R₁,C₁) and (R₂,C₂) are two minimal pairs, what can we say about the intersection (R₁∩R₂, C₁∩C₂)? Is it necessarily a saddle pair?" Difficulty="6" Token="70" Rely="1,2"/>
<Step ID="4" Task="Suppose |R₁| < |R₂|. Can we construct a new saddle pair (R',C') where R' ⊆ R₂ and C' ⊆ C₂, but with fewer rows than R₂?" Difficulty="7" Token="80" Rely="1,2,3"/>
<Step ID="5" Task="If such a construction in Step 4 is possible, how does this contradict the minimality of (R₂,C₂)?" Difficulty="5" Token="60" Rely="4"/>
<Step ID="6" Task="If such a construction in Step 4 is impossible, can we prove that |R₁| must equal |R₂|?" Difficulty="6" Token="70" Rely="4"/>
<Step ID="7" Task="Using the results from the previous steps, how do we conclude that any two minimal pairs must contain the same number of rows?" Difficulty="5" Token="60" Rely="5,6"/>
</Plan>
```

