4. Calculate ΔH from ΔU using the formula ΔH = ΔU + ΔnRT, where Δn is the change in moles of gas
5. Calculate ΔH°_f(HgO) using Hess's Law: ΔH°_rxn = 2ΔH°_f(HgO) - 2ΔH°_f(Hg) - ΔH°_f(O₂)
6. Since ΔH°_f(O₂) = 0 by definition, solve for ΔH°_f(HgO)
7. Take the absolute value of the result to get |X|
